<article class="env-corollary" id="E08F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/E08F">Corollary <span data-tag="E08F">1.1.5.12</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a topological category. Then the topological nerve $\tNerve (\calC )$ is an $\infty $-category. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/1280" data-tag="1280">1.1.5.10</a>, since the singular complex of any topological space is a Kan complex. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>